==============================================================================
PART 3.  The increment representation of the SAME driven ring.
         sigma preserved EXACTLY; E collapses to 0.
==============================================================================
  Y_t = X_t - X_{t-1} mod 4, read as +-1 (an increment IS an odd variable)
    position  repr:  sigma = 0.831776616672   E = 0.885891937582
    increment repr:  sigma_A = 0.000000000000  sigma_B = 0.831776616672  E = 0.000e+00
    sigma_B(increments) - sigma(positions) = -1.110e-16
  -> EXACTLY EQUAL.  A reduction that preserves the physical EPR while
     sending E to zero.  Canon Fig. DM(b) exhibits coarse-grainings where
     sigma and E collapse TOGETHER; this one does not.  Scope conditions 1
     and 3 are therefore not independent.

==============================================================================
PART 4.  COUNTEREXAMPLE 2 -- the excluded-present split (E_gap).
         Canon states no split convention.
==============================================================================
  X_t = (U_t, U_{t+1}), U i.i.d. Bern(0.5).  pi = [0.25 0.25 0.25 0.25]
  E (contiguous) = I(X0;X1) = 0.693147180560  > 0
    E_gap at block length L=1: 0.000e+00
    E_gap at block length L=2: 0.000e+00
    E_gap at block length L=3: 0.000e+00
  sigma (Convention A) = inf
  -> +inf: the reverse of edge (u,v)->(v,w) exists only if w=u, so the
     forward path measure is not absolutely continuous w.r.t. its reverse.
  Under the excluded-present split: sigma > 0, E_gap = 0.  FALSE as stated.

